   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law and the tax law, in\nrelation to certificate of authority numbers",
    "basePrintNo": "S891",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S891-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§51, 53, 53-a, 54, 54-a & 55, ABC L (as proposed in S.4661 & A.6989); amd §1134, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S891\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law and the tax law, in\nrelation to certificate of authority numbers\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nc.367.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by directing the Depart-\nment of Taxation and Finance to establish a publicly accessible database\ncontaining the certificate of authority number.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter. It\ndirects the Department of Taxation and Finance to establish a publicly\naccessible database for individuals who need to search for the certif-\nicate of authority number. The underlying chapter directed the State\nLiquor Authority to amend forms to include this number on certain liquor\nlicenses to ease the reporting burden for beer wholesalers.\n\nIn approval message 64 of 2020, the Executive noted that requiring the\nState Liquor Authority to provide these numbers was not the most appro-\npriate course. Instead, as the Department of Taxation and Finance\ncreates the certificate of authority number, they will establish the\ndatabase by 2022.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 367 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2020 amending the alcoholic beverage control law\nrelating to requiring certain licenses to brew or sell beer to include\nthe certificate of authority number as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.4661 and A.6889 takes effect.\n",
